#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# numerical_order

#% text
# `numerical_order(a, b)` gives 1 when `a` is numerically smaller than `b`, -1 when it is larger and 0 when they are equal. Complex numbers are compared by their real parts, then by the size of their imaginary parts; a comparison that cannot be decided gives 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
numerical_order(3/2, 1)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
numerical_order(3/2, 1.5)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
numerical_order(pi, e^2)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
sort([pi, 3, e, -inf, 2/3], numerical_order)
#% output
#= [-inf, 2/3, e, 3, pi]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `order`, `numerical_sort`, `sort`
